Bring the Marvell network processor out of reset on Sophos XGS appliances.

On these boards every front port belongs to a Marvell CN913x coprocessor behind a PCIe
endpoint, and that coprocessor comes out of power-on held in reset by a USB-to-SPI bridge whose
factory pin state is "held". The vendor firmware releases it during its own startup. Without
that step the coprocessor never boots, its serial console never says a word, and the appliance
has no network interfaces at all.

This plugin performs that release on every boot, before anything expects interfaces to exist.
The pin values are per board model and are read from the bridge's own EEPROM, so it acts only
on hardware it recognises and does nothing at all on anything else.

It also ships the kernel module that completes the handshake the coprocessor waits for, as
source, to be built and loaded deliberately rather than automatically.

